# Two-Phase Commit — ε-sensitive vote-order witness
# 
# "At some point, P3 was prepared while P2's last action (in the prev state)
#  was still its yes-vote (i.e., P2 had NOT yet transitioned to prepared)."
# 
# Each transaction's vote events are VC-concurrent (participants work in parallel
# during phase 1 — no messages between them). The prepared_Pi events overwrite
# the vote_yes_Pi labels on each participant's maximal frontier event.
# 
# Whether a linearization exists in which prepared_P3 fires BEFORE prepared_P2
# depends entirely on ε, because their timestamp gap is 0.25s.
# 
# Existential EPLTL verdict:
#   ε >= 0.25 → SATISFIED    (prepared_P3 and prepared_P2 are PO-concurrent;
#                             can interleave so P2's max label is still vote_yes_P2
#                             when prepared_P3 fires)
#   ε <  0.25 → VIOLATED     (time pins prepared_P2 ≺ prepared_P3 everywhere;
#                             at prepared_P3's state, @vote_yes_P2 is always false)
TRUE S (prepared_P3 & @vote_yes_P2)
